{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Parent\n\nEpic `77e3-28e2-31ec-47ec`, authorized at full scope by the operator on 2026-11-02.\nThis is deliverable 1 plus the net-mechanism half of deliverable 3 (its red proof).\n\n## The gap\n\n`scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py` is a shrink-only ratchet over\n`.github/mechanism-baseline.json`. It censuses seven mechanism kinds — `lock`, `env_var`,\n`config_key`, `feature_flag`, `ci_gate`, `autouse_fixture`, `test_helper` — and fails on\nany `new>0`. A new mechanism is admitted by an in-tree marker\n`# mechanism-ok: <kind> <name> — <reason or ticket id>` at the definition site.\n\nMeasured at `origin/main` `4cf1ae42946`:\n\n- Bucketing is `scripts/_mechanism_delta/compare.py:34-49`.\n- The exit decision is `compare.py:99` — `return (1 if (new_bad or inc_bad or errors) else 0), lines`.\n  `counters.stale` is never consulted, which is what makes removal always pass.\n- A `new` key carrying a nonblank marker passes at `compare.py:89-92`; a blank reason is an\n  error at `compare.py:83`.\n- The marker grammar is `scripts/_mechanism_delta/markers.py:20` (`_MARKER_RE`), with\n  separators `(\"—\", \"--\", \"-\", \":\")` at `markers.py:23` and the capture at `markers.py:42-43`.\n  The parser has exactly three fields — kind, name, reason. Nothing parses a retirement.\n\nSo the ratchet asks \"is this mechanism justified?\" and never \"is the system net-simpler\nafterward?\". A plan may add a mechanism, write a one-line reason, and pass with nothing\nretired.\n\nPlan review does not close the gap. `A1` is the only complexity criterion and is advisory:\n`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/criteria_routing.json:814-815` carries `\"block_threshold\": 0.95`\nand `\"default_posture\": \"advisory\"`. An advisory criterion cannot block.\n\n## The change\n\nA new BLOCKING plan-review criterion, `project.net-mechanism`. A plan whose edit set adds a\nmechanism of a kind the ratchet counts must either name the mechanism it retires, or carry\nan explicit justification for why no retirement is possible. Absent both, it blocks.\n\nThe criterion reasons about the PLAN, not the tree. It runs at claim time, before any code\nexists, so it judges what the plan says it will add against what it says it will remove.\n\n## Route: project overlay, not a packaged criterion\n\nMeasured at `origin/main`. `project.portability` is a BLOCKING criterion that lives\nentirely in the repo-root overlay:\n\n- `.rebar/criteria_routing.json:3-15` — `\"default_posture\": \"blocking\"`,\n  `\"block_threshold\": 0.9`, `\"exec\": \"1-TURN\"`, `\"facet\": \"project-invariants\"`.\n- `.rebar/criteria_routing.json:130-132` — its `activate` entry naming `plan_review`.\n- `.rebar/prompts/plan-review-project-portability.md` — the rubric.\n- It is ABSENT from `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/registry.py` (not in `CANONICAL_LLM` at\n  `registry.py:87`) and ABSENT from `docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md`.\n\nFour plan-review overlay criteria already ship this way (`project.portability`,\n`project.symbol-reference-completeness`, `project.engine-layer-enforcement`,\n`project.measurement-provenance`), so the route has precedent, not just feasibility.\n\nThe overlay route is chosen for two reasons, both on the epic's own terms:\n\n1. **Scope correctness.** The criterion's trigger is rebar's own seven-kind mechanism\n   census, defined by `scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py` and\n   `.github/mechanism-baseline.json`. A downstream consumer of rebar has neither. A\n   packaged criterion would fire on plans in projects with no such taxonomy.\n2. **Net complexity.** The overlay route touches 3 files. The packaged route would\n   additionally require editing `CANONICAL_LLM` at `registry.py:87`, satisfying\n   `check_registry_coverage` at `registry.py:536` and `validate_packaged_routing()` at\n   `registry.py:564`, and regenerating `docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md` via\n   `python -m rebar.llm.plan_review.registry regenerate-criteria-guide` to satisfy\n   `validate_criteria_guide` at `criteria_guide.py:89`. Adding six files of surface inside\n   a complexity-reduction epic would invite `A1` on its own deliverable.\n\nREJECTED ALTERNATIVE, recorded so it is not re-litigated: a packaged criterion in\n`CANONICAL_LLM`. Rejected for the two reasons above.\n\nThe overlay accepts a `project.`-prefixed net-new id. `src/rebar/llm/criteria/overlay.py:360-368`\nrejects a `project.`-prefixed id that collides with a built-in, and `overlay.py:371-376`\nrejects an un-prefixed net-new id; `project.net-mechanism` is neither.\n\n## Files this change touches\n\n1. `.rebar/prompts/plan-review-project-net-mechanism.md` — NEW. The rubric. Front matter is\n   the six keys parsed by `parse_front_matter`: `schema_version`, `title`, `description`,\n   `execution_mode`, `category`, `dimension`.\n2. `.rebar/criteria_routing.json` — a routing entry plus an `activate` entry listing\n   `plan_review`.\n3. `tests/unit/test_project_net_mechanism_criterion.py` — NEW, modeled on\n   `tests/unit/test_project_portability_criterion.py` (274 lines).\n\nThe prompt id is derived, not chosen: `src/rebar/llm/criteria/ids.py:42` computes\n`f\"{prefix}{criterion_id.replace('.', '-')}\"`, so `project.net-mechanism` resolves to\n`plan-review-project-net-mechanism` and fixes the rubric filename.\n\nWording constraint: `scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py` scans\n`src/rebar/llm/reviewers` and `src/rebar/_guides` (`:56`). The new rubric sits under\n`.rebar/prompts/`, outside that scan, so no allowlist row is needed. The rubric will still\navoid the banned `success criteri(a|on)` family (`:21`) and bare `SC`/`SCs` (`:22`) so the\nwording stays consistent with packaged rubrics.\n\n## Portability\n\nPer the blocking `project.portability` criterion, a check whose only trigger is a specific\nCI system is not portable. This criterion runs inside plan review, an operation-linked\nin-process path with no CI dependency. It reads the plan text, never the CI environment and\nnever the ratchet script. It therefore fires identically with no CI provider configured.\n\n## Provider neutrality\n\nrebar must support a wide variety of providers and models. The rubric is `exec: 1-TURN`,\nthe same single-turn prompt form every packaged criterion and `project.portability` use. It\nnames no vendor, assumes no vendor-specific tool-calling syntax, and depends on no\nmodel-specific capability.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `registry.effective_criteria(REPO_ROOT)` contains `project.net-mechanism`, and\n      `registry.effective_routing(REPO_ROOT)[\"project.net-mechanism\"][\"default_posture\"]`\n      is `\"blocking\"`. Verified by a test.\n- [ ] The rubric resolves through the production loader:\n      `prompts.get_prompt(criterion_prompt_id(\"project.net-mechanism\"), repo_root=REPO_ROOT)`\n      returns a non-empty body, and `parse_front_matter` yields all six keys. Verified by a\n      test.\n- [ ] `route_criteria` returns `project.net-mechanism` for a plan in its declared scope.\n      Verified by a test.\n- [ ] RED PROOF: a plan that adds a mechanism, names no retired mechanism, and carries no\n      justification is scored as a finding by this criterion. Verified against a named\n      ticket from the breaking pass that landed a mechanism and should have been caught.\n      The ticket id is recorded in the test.\n- [ ] A plan that adds a mechanism AND names the mechanism it retires produces no finding.\n      Verified by a test.\n- [ ] A plan that adds no mechanism produces no finding — the criterion does not fire on\n      unrelated plans. Verified by a test.\n- [ ] The criterion fires with no CI provider present. Verified by a test that exercises it\n      with no CI environment configured.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes.\n\n## Measurement base\n\nEvery citation above was read from `origin/main` at `4cf1ae42946` via\n`git show origin/main:<path>`. Line numbers are from that commit. Citations were measured\nindividually, not sampled."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793649637301860931,"uuid":"2325ffab-944d-4f7e-a08a-afd9035dcce0"}